+### 2.5 Crossing Conflict Area and Deferred Entry Landmark
 
+The **crossing conflict area (CCA)** is the stretch of railway alignment within the road-and-pedestrian crossing corridor, bounded along the direction of travel by an **entry boundary** and the **exit plane** of §2.4(1). **Only the exit plane is documented.** The entry landmark is **DEFERRED (RD-006)**: this protocol neither invents a landmark nor asserts that the entry boundary mirrors the exit plane. Until the researcher states it, $T_2$ and any duration anchored on it remain unevaluable. No coordinates, distances or survey are implied.
